  "title": "Jose Rizal",
  "summary": "Jose Rizal, a physician and writer born in Calamba, Laguna, on 19 June 1861, wrote Noli Me Tangere condemning Spanish colonial rule and was exiled to Dapitan, Mindanao, after returning to the Philippines in 1892. A military court convicted him of sedition and he was shot by firing squad in Manila on 30 December 1896; his death filled the Katipunan rebels with new determination.",
